 "title": "Hilbert's tenth problem",
 "statement": {
  "text": "Hilbert's tenth problem is the tenth on the list of mathematical problems that the German mathematician David Hilbert posed in 1900. It is the challenge to provide a general algorithm that, for any given Diophantine equation, can decide whether the equation has a solution with all unknowns taking integer values.",
  "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilbert's_tenth_problem",
